//BUG="a return inside a while is treated as enough, though the loop may run zero times"
//ERR any

// The only `ret` is inside a `while`, and the condition is false on entry here,
// so the loop body never runs and the function falls off the end. A loop is not
// a guarantee: unless its condition is the literal `true`, the code after it is
// reachable and the function still needs a return there.
//
// 05_functions/28_a_loop_followed_by_a_return.cpl is the accepted form, and
// 05_functions/29_while_true_returns_from_inside.cpl is the one loop that does
// count.

fn f n
    while n > 0
        ret 1

fn main
    out "{f(0)}"
